ent for students with disabilities with a comparison group of students with disabilities. Specifically, the researchers attempt to answer the following questions:\n\n1. Is there a significant difference in achievement on mean standardized science scores for students with disabilities in SWH classrooms when conducting pre-intervention and postintervention comparisons? 2. Is there a significant difference in achievement on mean standardized science scores for students with disabilities in SWH classrooms when conducting post-intervention comparisons with a comparison group? 3. Do students with",
