      "snippet": {
        "text": "In response to these challenges, educational researchers and practitioners have been exploring innovative teaching methods that can enhance the effectiveness of science education at the primary level.Quantum teaching is one such innovative approach that has gained attention for its potential to revolutionize the way science is taught in primary schools.\n\nThe concept of \"quantum teaching\" represents a novel and innovative approach to pedagogy (Lastasa & Habaridota, 2020).This approach draws inspiration from the principles of quantum physics, which emphasize the interconnectedness, uncertainty, and transformative potential of learning (Scerri, 2019) (Ritchhart & Perkins, 2005).Quantum teaching aims to introduce a dynamic and learner-centric model into primary school science education (Burkhart, 2016).It seeks to create an environment where students become active participants in their learning journey, encouraging them to explore, question, and discover the wonders of science (Roussou, 2004) (Grabinger & Dunlap, 1995) (Chin & Brown, 2002).By harnessing the principles of quantum teaching, educators aim to address the existing challenges in primary school science education and, in doing so, improve learning achievement (Adams et al., 2018).This approach not only focuses on the transmission of knowledge but also emphasizes student engagement, inquiry-based learning, and the exploration of the interconnectedness of scientific phenomena (Holton, 2017).\n\nHowever, despite the theoretical promise of quantum teaching, there is limited empirical research on its application and effectiveness in the context of primary school science education (Peters, 2013) (Klichowski, 2017).To address this gap and better understand the potential impact of quantum teaching on learning achievement, this research project seeks to investigate the following questions (Shannon & Bylsma, 2002): Can quantum teaching strategies be effectively implemented in primary school science classrooms?What are the effects of quantum teaching on students' learning achievement and their attitudes toward science?Are there specific challenges and considerations associated with integrating quantum teaching into primary school science education?\n\nThis research aims to contribute to the ongoing discourse on innovative pedagogical approaches in primary school science education and provide valuable insights for educators, policymakers, and researchers seeking to improve learning achievement and foster a lifelong love of science among young learners.",
