        "text": "Artificial intelligence-based tutoring software or intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) are capable of handling individualized feedback and guidance for one-on-one education. They cannot take the role of teachers, though, as they are unable to impart knowledge in the same way that humans can. When human tutors are not accessible for brief courses that can be given and assessed online, they can be useful. It can be used to teach languages, geography, circuits, medical diagnostics, computer programming, mathematics, physics, genetics, chemistry, and other subjects in e-learning platforms. They are made with engagement, grading criteria, and comprehension in mind.",
