        "text": "AI tools are increasingly being used in education to improve learning and teaching methods (T. Wang & Cheng, 2021). However, there is still an unresolved issue about the openness of the created data. Typically, when AI technologies are utilized to involve users in a specific learning task, users are expected to provide consent, indicating their agreement with the terms of technology use and the collection, management, and processing of their data (Nguyen et al., 2023). \n\nAI progress in education can revolutionize the educational environment and impact the role of all stakeholders. Recently, AI technologies have been increasingly used to improve our comprehension of students' learning and to increase learning outcomes and experiences. The implementation of AI has resulted in increasing ethical hazards and worries related to several areas, such as personal data and learner independence (Nguyen et al., 2023). In several ways, AI has revolutionized formal education. With artificial intelligence, students' performance data are analyzed and adapted to their individual needs. As a result, learning has become more efficient and effective. Teachers and students benefit from intelligent tutoring systems powered by artificial intelligence, which provides immediate feedback and guidance. With AI, adaptive assessments are created that adapt to students' performance. Teachers may concentrate more on teaching by using AI to automate administrative duties such as attendance scheduling and grading. Teachers can keep an eye on their students' progress, offer criticism, and respond to their inquiries with the help of AI-powered assistants. AI generates practice questions, summaries, and quizzes as well as personalized learning materials. The learning process is ongoing and lifelong since AI monitors students' progress and modifies learning paths accordingly (Alam, 2023). \n\nAlam (Alam, 2023) investigated how AI and other contemporary technologies are enhancing student education and being incorporated into curricula and classrooms. The researcher mentioned that students can adapt learning experiences to their needs and skill levels and provide instant feedback. Furthermore, allowing interaction with virtual settings and simulations may provide students with immersive learning experiences. On online learning platforms, students can enroll in courses worldwide and take advantage of educational resources, as well as technologically enhanced teaching strategies tailored to their learning styles, goals, and speeds. The use of game-like elements makes studying more participatory and interesting for students. Moreover, AI has changed traditional education.",
